# Discord Provider

Manage Discord servers as code: settings, roles, channels, permission overwrites, member roles, webhooks, invites,
messages and emojis.

The provider talks to the Discord REST API with a bot token. It does not connect to the gateway.

## Setup

1. Create an application in the [Discord Developer Portal](https://discord.com/developers/applications) and add a bot.
2. Copy the bot token. Pass it as the provider's `token`, or set the `DISCORD_TOKEN` environment variable. The `Bot `
   prefix is optional.
3. Invite the bot to your server with the permissions it needs to manage the resources you declare. The bot can
   only manage roles below its own highest role. A permission overwrite can only grant permissions the bot itself
   has, unless the bot has Administrator.
4. Username lookups in the `discord_member` data source need the **Server Members Intent**, which you enable on the
   bot's settings page.

